{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm","id":866416,"title":"Question about the Battleground realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-16T09:27:22-07:00","id":866416,"title":"Question about the Battleground realm","content":"I'm running a Werewolf game, and my players need to go into the Battleground realm to view an old battle. The main book describes that you can potentially get hints of an upcoming battle. I planned on taking this one step further. Would it be completely out of the realm of possibility for them to see part of a very large future battle they will be apart of as sort of a &quot;Potential future&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:08:48-07:00","id":866428,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:45:59-07:00","id":866449,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Sounds good<br /> <br /> But I'd either drive them crazy with 7 or 8 potential ways it could go, or have critical details hidden in fog.<br /> <br /> <br /> A question on the Realm ive had for a while, is their a good book to get ideas for statting up a tank, ship or plane, might be relevant in battleground if you visit vietnam, civil war, or world wars,<br /> <br /> As well in modern times I could See pentex Sending an APC out to destroy a caern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-16-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T12:55:15-07:00","id":866499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=866449#post866449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,<br /> <br /> As well in modern times I could See pentex Sending an APC out to destroy a caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the dumb way to destroy a caern, but someone might try, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T19:25:33-07:00","id":866612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=866499#post866499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be the dumb way to destroy a caern, but someone might try, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the U.S. a number of modified APC vehicles have been sold to police departments. I could easily see a scenario where a Pentex sub division has access to an APC. And while using it in a Caern assault might be a bit much using it to assault a kinfolk compound is well within the Realm of possibility.<br /> Of course the opposite is also true Garou are well suited to &quot;domestic terrorism&quot; and stealing a city's SWAT team's APC and using it to breach a Pentex facility would be stupid, but could be effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:35:32-07:00","id":866639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=866612#post866612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the U.S. a number of modified APC vehicles have been sold to police departments. I could easily see a scenario where a Pentex sub division has access to an APC. And while using it in a Caern assault might be a bit much using it to assault a kinfolk compound is well within the Realm of possibility.<br /> Of course the opposite is also true Garou are well suited to &quot;domestic terrorism&quot; and stealing a city's SWAT team's APC and using it to breach a Pentex facility would be stupid, but could be effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd still attract way more attention than buying up the properties around it, setting up stripmalls and the like, and then writing off the loss when no one visits the new tracts by the spooky woods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:35:35-07:00","id":866640,"title":"","content":"I think Saur is saying that is dumb because an APC is not going to be a significant obstacle to a group of highly-motivated werewolves. There are better ways to fight Garou on their home turf.<br /> <br /> I would hate to be the mockeries huddling inside that thing as it rolled into the bawn...<br /> <br /> Edit: beaten to the punch. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:38:25-07:00","id":866641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=866640#post866640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Saur is saying that is dumb because an APC is not going to be a significant obstacle to a group of highly-motivated werewolves.<br /> <br /> I would hate to be the mockeries huddling inside that thing as it rolled into the bawn...</div> </div> </div> </div>That, too; Jam Weapons, Jam Technology, and Gremlins mean that APCs and any armaments might just stop functioning at a moment's notice. Better hope your fomori powers included night vision, natural weapons, sturdiness, and armor, or else you're going to get sliced up like a zoanoid extra against a late-series Guyver.<br /> <br /> (Direct threats are the things that Garou fare the best against. Give them one, and you'll see it torn to pieces.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T09:19:18-07:00","id":866868,"title":"","content":"Id agree, its dumb... but when has that ever kept someone from doing something...<br /> <br /> an idea? Some disgraced American military, ideally an american Jingoist, joins pentexes first teams, but while competent a major part of his concerns, is that he see's the garou as &quot;Un american&quot; for this or that reason.<br /> <br /> based on the Colonel from the movie &quot;Avatar&quot; (Im sorry if some people have fond feelings for him not trying to step on your toes) <br /> <br /> sounds like a good way to get an APC for a pack to fight.<br /> <br /> and in Battleground, ideas what the armor and weapons on the tanks used in vietnam or the world wars, should be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:19:22-07:00","id":867769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=866868#post866868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Id agree, its dumb... but when has that ever kept someone from doing something...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this sums up perfectly how I treat NPCs in my game. I have no problem giving the pack a challenge that they have to out think. Or maybe something that CAN put up a strong fight just so they can really put their full strength to some fun use. And then they'll have NPCs who are just not the brightest. Not every enemy is always smart, strong, or even a real credible threat. I think driving an APC at the pack or even a Caern could be incredibly fun. Will they likely die horribly? Of course. Is that sometimes the fun part of being a Werewolf? I certainly think so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:52:47-07:00","id":867836,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's a billion reasons to use an APC when attacking a caern. Most of them are pretty dumb, but a lot of cases where you'd need to conceal a nasty thing seem legit. Like &quot;they've got some nasty balefire-type thing on board and don't want the Garou to see it until they're already shredding their way through metal&quot;. Or &quot;It looks important and also easy to destroy, which means it gets everyone's attention&quot;. Suicide missions exist after all, especially when the people assigned to them don't quite realize what the Garou can do to an APC. Or maybe there's a pack of Spirals onboard! (Whose pack HASN'T driven a van through a chain link fence to attack by surprise?)<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's mounting a heavy machine gun with some very custom bullets. Yeah, that's more Shadowrun than World of Darkness, but there's gotta be a First Team out there equipped with gigantic silver bullets, held in reserve for when they need to stop a Garou ritual RIGHT NOW. You wouldn't want to lead with it, but after the Fomori and some Spirals rush the caern, that kind of firepower is the last thing the Gaians would want to crash onto the scene. Maybe at the end of a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:21:58-07:00","id":867854,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on how to stat such a thing, or a WW 1 or 2 Tank up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T17:08:56-07:00","id":867927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=867854#post867854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thoughts on how to stat such a thing, or a WW 1 or 2 Tank up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vehicles appear in Rage Across the Amazon and the Vampire 2nd editions player's guide. It's actually quite possible - and maybe even a bit easy! - to breach some of them just by clawing them, and there's always fur gnarl for the ones that are more difficult. However, an APC only requires ten levels at difficulty 4 to tear open under this system; this won't result in total destruction, but it will be a pretty big hole slashed through the armor.<br /> <br /> The higher end of difficulty for breaching is a main battle tank, requiring 18 damage successes at difficulty 8. Those are much less likely to show up, however, unless your caern is in an active war zone where relatively higher-profile hardware is being deployed. Even then, three successes on a roll with Gremlins will still turn it into an oddly-shaped bunker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:03:26-07:00","id":868039,"title":"","content":"Would I be better getting Arage across the Amazon, or whichever &quot; Rage across the world&quot; Its in in your opinion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:10:12-07:00","id":868093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=868039#post868039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would I be better getting Arage across the Amazon, or whichever &quot; Rage across the world&quot; Its in in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAtA has some vehicles, but not many, and the rules for breaching vehicles aren't actually there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T21:00:52-07:00","id":868148,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on the Idea of a fanatical Jingoist, as the man behind the assault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:01:10-07:00","id":868521,"title":"","content":"Could be fun to ham it up and have Sargent Killbutt chew the scenery, but you are basically describing the villain from Fern Gully.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T08:39:22-07:00","id":882896,"title":"","content":"Wait how was Hexus a Jingoist, Jingoist means, fanatical even violent nationlism.<br /> <br /> And I think a Fanatical american Zealout could See the Garou's ideals as Anathema.<br /> <br /> Also reason I was checking on this thread again, Just noticed I should get &quot;Rage across the world&quot; anthologys, including &quot;Rage across the Amazon, as part of my kickstarter reward, for shattered dreamsany idea when those PDFS go out? or do I need to keep checking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:28:34-07:00","id":884391,"title":"","content":"On the subject of adversaries using an APC (or other similarly light armored vehicle) against werewolves, I have my own $.02 I'd like to add to the pot. I bristle a little bit at the broad statement that using APCs against werewolves is stupid and would <i>never</i> work. I'd instead point out that tactical use of such equipment requires adherence to doctrine that has been painstakingly learned over the last sixty years or so.<br /> <br /> 1. Speed is life. The quote is actually attributed to Oswald Bolke, a First World War German fighter ace who was talking about airplanes... but the concept applies nicely to maneuver warfare too. In short, anything that stays still (and can't hide) on a battlefield is pretty much dead. Even a main battle tank -- if it gets disabled -- is in some serious sh**. As such, you generally don't see APCs outside of flat, open terrain (the recent conflict in Afghanistan being a glaring, rare, and controversial exception).<br /> <br /> 2. Armored vehicles are supposed to fight at standoff ranges. Close quarters is where the APC's greatest weakness lies. Now you <i>do</i> see their use in urban combat... but that's mainly because of the well developed road networks that you usually find in urban terrain. Even then they tend to get picked off a lot.<br /> <br /> 3. The most dangerous thing about an armored personnel carrier is not the carrier, but the <i>personnel</i>. The real purpose of the APC is to get the troops to where they need to go quickly and with a minimum of casualties en-route. Once at the point of contact however, the <i>whole idea</i> is to dismount your troops so <i>they</i> can do the actual fighting. (In recent times -- specifically Iraq -- there was a move away from dismounting troops for force protection reasons in favor of &quot;Thunder Runs&quot;, but this was highly controversial, not terribly effective, in some cases counterproductive, and at any rate, really signaled a worrisome lack of strategy).<br /> <br /> So if your First Team / fomori / Dead Man's Hand or <i>whatever</i>, is fighting the Garou in, like, <i>Kansas</i> or somewhere -- it <i>could</i> work. Just so long as they keep their distance (Jam Technology has a limited range), make liberal use of ranged weapons, and always, <i>always</i> keep moving. That said, if you look at the basic doctrine, the APC is precisely the wrong choice for fighting the Garou even conceptually. First off, werewolves (and especially the prize jewels -- caerns) tend to be found in the deep wilderness. Such broken terrain robs motorized transport of its most valuable trait: Mobility. (As an example, you don't see many pictures of APCs or tanks from the Vietnam Conflict). The deep forest also inhibits the use of standoff weapons, since for the most part, you can't hit what you can't see. As such, (and this is another reason why you didn't see them used much in Vietnam) most such combat will be a close range -- tactically the worst situation you can get since the APC is at its weakest at close quarters while werewolves are at their strongest. Lastly, since the whole purpose of the APC is to get your dismounts into combat, using APCs to somehow change the equation when your leg-infantry is basically little more than fodder to a Garou warrior -- is really doing nothing more than bringing new meaning to the term &quot;meals on wheels&quot;.<br /> <br /> But some idiot adversary who's watched too many Michael Bay movies and whose tactical expertise mainly stems from playing Call of Duty a lot? Sure. That could be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T23:34:56-07:00","id":884414,"title":"","content":"Keeping your distance from a potentially invisible enemy is easier said than done; Jam Technology might have a limited range, but stealth Gifts and cutting through the Umbra can still put you close enough to use them. Hell, you might even be able to touch them without being noticed, which, if you have Gremlins, means that the APC is at least tactically bricked and might end up permanently so.<br /> <br /> Kansas, however, has a feature that some caerns might harness to make use of any force against them a potential hand-in-blender situation, and that's the dry line, along with attendant spirits associated with destructive weather. One twister moving through is all you need to give a paramilitary raiding force a very, very bad day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016