red personnel carrier is not the carrier, but the <i>personnel</i>. The real purpose of the APC is to get the troops to where they need to go quickly and with a minimum of casualties en-route. Once at the point of contact however, the <i>whole idea</i> is to dismount your troops so <i>they</i> can do the actual fighting. (In recent times -- specifically Iraq -- there was a move away from dismounting troops for force protection reasons in favor of &quot;Thunder Runs&quot;, but this was highly controversial, not terribly effective, in some cases counterproductive, and at any rate, really signaled a worrisome lack of strategy).<br /> <br /> So if your First Team / fomori / Dead Man's Hand or <i>whatever</i>, is fighting the Garou in, like, <i>Kansas</i> or somewhere -- it <i>could</i> work. Just so long as they keep their distance (Jam Technology has a limited range), make liberal use of ranged weapons, and always, <i>always</i> keep moving. That said, if you look at the basic doctrine, the APC is precisely the wrong choice for fighting the Garou even conceptually. First off, werewolves (and especially the prize jewels -- caerns) tend to be found in the deep wilderness. Such broken terrain robs motorized transport of its most valuable trait: Mobility. (As an example, you don't see many pictures of APCs or tanks from the Vietnam Conflict). The deep forest also inhibits the use of standoff weapons, since for the most part, you can't hit what you can't see. As such, (and this is another reason why you didn't see them used much in Vietnam) most such combat will be a close range -- tactically the worst situation you can get since the APC is at its weakest at close quarters while werewolves are at their strongest. Lastly, since the whole purpose of the APC is to get your dismounts into combat, using APCs to somehow change the equation when your leg-infantry is basically little more than fodder to a Garou warrior -- is really doing nothing more than bringing new meaning to the term &quot;meals on wheels&quot;.<br /> <br /> But some idiot adversary who's watched too many Michael Bay movies and whose tactical expertise mainly stems from playing Call of Duty a lot? Sure. That could be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> so you dont think its the kind of stupid a Flag waving American Cultural Zealout, thinking with military experience, would be that likely to display?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-07-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:42:05-07:00","id":884864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=884414#post884414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping your distance from a potentially invisible enemy is easier said than done; Jam Technology might have a limited range, but stealth Gifts and cutting through the Umbra can still put you close enough to use them. Hell, you might even be able to touch them without being noticed, which, if you have Gremlins, means that the APC is at least tactically bricked and might end up permanently so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but if you cannot detect your target in the first place, the presence or absence of motorized transport does nothing to alter the tactical equation (having the APC doesn't hurt you in any way, in other words). On the flip side, if you remain mobile (say, you have a <i>general</i> idea of your adversary's position), your werewolf adversary will probably have a harder time getting at you if you're zipping around the battlefield at 40 MPH, than if you're on foot. Moreover, the longer you draw out that little stalemate, the more Gnosis the werewolf has to expend to <i>stay</i> invisible. So long as his Gnosis runs out before your gas does, the APC is an advantage rather than a hindrance.<br /> <br /> And if the werewolves in question are <i>that</i> good at being undetectable, how exactly are you anywhere within a hundred miles of their caern in the first place?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=884414#post884414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One twister moving through is all you need to give a paramilitary raiding force a very, very bad day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but if you're going up against a sept of werewolves who can summon up a tornado against you, would you rather go through that in the open on foot, or in a large, heavy, armored vehicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:15:33-07:00","id":884894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm#post866416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a Werewolf game, and my players need to go into the Battleground realm to view an old battle. The main book describes that you can potentially get hints of an upcoming battle. I planned on taking this one step further. Would it be completely out of the realm of possibility for them to see part of a very large future battle they will be apart of as sort of a &quot;Potential future&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But to keep things from being seen fully, have there be 3+ ways it could go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:34:10-07:00","id":884914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=884864#post884864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but if you cannot detect your target in the first place, the presence or absence of motorized transport does nothing to alter the tactical equation (having the APC doesn't hurt you in any way, in other words). On the flip side, if you remain mobile (say, you have a <i>general</i> idea of your adversary's position), your werewolf adversary will probably have a harder time getting at you if you're zipping around the battlefield at 40 MPH, than if you're on foot. Moreover, the longer you draw out that little stalemate, the more Gnosis the werewolf has to expend to <i>stay</i> invisible. So long as his Gnosis runs out before your gas does, the APC is an advantage rather than a hindrance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could run into an invisible JT zone and end up suddenly getting your steering and propulsion shut down. Badger's Burrow helps a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if the werewolves in question are <i>that</i> good at being undetectable, how exactly are you anywhere within a hundred miles of their caern in the first place? </div> </div> </div>Well, it does take time to get somewhere, even if you're fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, but if you're going up against a sept of werewolves who can summon up a tornado against you, would you rather go through that in the open on foot, or in a large, heavy, armored vehicle? </div> </div> </div>Either way, it's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2sEtFwzxJ6I\" target=\"_blank\">game over, man! Game over!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:47:34-07:00","id":885007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=884914#post884914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could run into an invisible JT zone and end up suddenly getting your steering and propulsion shut down. Badger's Burrow helps a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that any different from anti-tank mines or IEDs? Anti-vehicle mines have been around as long as militaries have been using vehicles. It didn't spell the end of maneuver warfare in World War II, so why would it be any different in this scenario just because this time it's werewolves doing it instead of humans? By in large, static defenses like that are rarely effective in practice since they either have to be grotesquely broad (a violation of Sun Tzu's maxim that &quot;he who defends everything, defends nothing&quot; and as such is generally vulnerable to concentrated penetration and breakout), or is simply isolated or bypassed. In the former case, the Garou simply don't have the resources to man a broad defensive front in the first place. In the second case, if the Garou want to keep from simply getting bypassed, they'd have to set up their defenses so close to their caern that an approaching adversary (assuming, of course that the caern's location is known to at least a general degree) can simply dance around them until the Garou Theurges run out of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=884914#post884914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, it's game over, man! Game over!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that a tornado can't knock over an armored vehicle, but it's much harder than with a tractor-trailer rig which is extremely light compared to its sail area. Also, if I was going to have to decide which vehicle I was going to have wind-blown debris shooting into (with me inside it at the time), I'm picking the thing with armor. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:16:15-07:00","id":885021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885007#post885007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that any different from anti-tank mines or IEDs? Anti-vehicle mines have been around as long as militaries have been using vehicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a distinct lack of magically silent vehicle shutdowns in military history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It didn't spell the end of maneuver warfare in World War II, so why would it be any different in this scenario just because this time it's werewolves doing it instead of humans? </div> </div> </div>Because their bag of tricks is substantially broader. Magically so, even. We're talking ghosting through the vehicle to making it turn on people, Maximum Overdrive style. Military doctrine does not account for being stuck in a monster movie where the laws of physics bend and flow to make things easier for the monster..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By in large, static defenses like that are rarely effective in practice since they either have to be grotesquely broad (a violation of Sun Tzu's maxim that &quot;he who defends everything, defends nothing&quot; and as such is generally vulnerable to concentrated penetration and breakout), or is simply isolated or bypassed. In the former case, the Garou simply don't have the resources to man a broad defensive front in the first place. In the second case, if the Garou want to keep from simply getting bypassed, they'd have to set up their defenses so close to their caern that an approaching adversary (assuming, of course that the caern's location is known to at least a general degree) can simply dance around them until the Garou Theurges run out of Gnosis. </div> </div> </div>They don't exactly need to, since they have scrying and invisible guards on their side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not that a tornado can't knock over an armored vehicle, but it's much harder than with a tractor-trailer rig which is extremely light compared to its sail area. Also, if I was going to have to decide which vehicle I was going to have wind-blown debris shooting into (with me inside it at the time), I'm picking the thing with armor. Just saying. </div> </div> </div>That was a rather small tornado. Larger ones, the likes of which Garou would probably aim to call up, would likely turn an APC into a flying coffin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:05:53-07:00","id":885497,"title":"","content":"oh a vaguely related question?<br /> <br /> how do you think Garou will view psychic kinfolk? as curiousitys, or as potentially dangerous wild cards?<br /> <br /> or pentex, with its massive programs devoted to finding and using psychics... ideas on how to incorporate them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:40:05-07:00","id":885530,"title":"","content":"Pentex i see like some TV shows various governmental institutions in relation to those with numina.. You either work FOR Them, or you are too 'dangerous' to be allowed to live and get hunted mercilessly. <br /> Garou i would think would have mixed reactions to kin with it.. Some would be ok, others might be scared, while others still might be 'kill it!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:29:54-07:00","id":885584,"title":"","content":"ouch Meant that question for other thread... sorry<br /> <br /> ideas on how well a Jingoistic (Fananitcal Nationalist) would fit into Pentex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:08:40-07:00","id":885623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885584#post885584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ouch Meant that question for other thread... sorry<br /> <br /> ideas on how well a Jingoistic (Fananitcal Nationalist) would fit into Pentex?</div> </div> </div> </div>They gave SAD Martin Fiske, so fairly well, apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T16:31:26-07:00","id":885775,"title":"","content":"Two things, take it you feel its believable that a flag waver, could see the Garou as &quot;Unamerican&quot; <br /> <br /> ok oh on shattered Dreams, think we'll get specialized backgrounds and merits? as it deserves special attention on resources...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T22:39:37-07:00","id":885969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885021#post885021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a distinct lack of magically silent vehicle shutdowns in military history.<br /> <br /> Because their bag of tricks is substantially broader. Magically so, even. We're talking ghosting through the vehicle to making it turn on people, Maximum Overdrive style. Military doctrine does not account for being stuck in a monster movie where the laws of physics bend and flow to make things easier for the monster..</div> </div> </div> </div>If the vehicle is a tactical kill, it's a tactical kill regardless of whether it hit a mine or hit a magical ward or whatever. The specific method of the kill is largely irrelevant. Dead is dead. An area-denial weapon (like a mine or an &quot;invisible JT trap&quot; the werewolves would use) represents fundamentally the same tactical challenge. Just because one is magic and the other isn't, how would that change the effect of battlefield doctrine? If you have a column and the vehicle in front suddenly blows up -- you stop and try to find another route around the minefield. If the vehicle instead stops suddenly and a bunch of werewolves appear out of thin air, rip the doors off the thing and <i>eat</i> the occupants -- well, probably best to go around that noise, right? Like, seriously. What's the difference?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885021#post885021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't exactly need to, since they have scrying and invisible guards on their side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what point you're trying to make. Can you expand upon that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885021#post885021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a rather small tornado. Larger ones, the likes of which Garou would probably aim to call up, would likely turn an APC into a flying coffin.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, would you rather go through that in the thing with armor, or out in the open on foot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T03:26:13-07:00","id":886074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885969#post885969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what point you're trying to make. Can you expand upon that?<br /> <br /> And again, would you rather go through that in the thing with armor, or out in the open on foot?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's talking about Spirits. Just because it's not easy to hide a Caern doesn't make it lightly defended by any stretch. However, the APC thing has gotten out of hand. If you want to storm a Caern you're sure as hell going to use any kind of machinery you can lay your hands on. Better to storm the place and move in quick. No one denies that the tactical paradigm is sound. The problem is that standard military methods of engagement aren't particularly useful when faced with horrifying monsters that laugh at small arms fire and can survive even some heavier stuff. Combine that with the superior lateral mobility and stealth of the Garou, and it quickly turns into the first encounter in Aliens (which game over, man, totally reminded me of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> So yeah. (Para)Military units will use APC's if they can get their hands on them. How much they will help them is a whole other kettle of fish.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:36:07-07:00","id":886163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/866416-question-about-the-battleground-realm?p=885969#post885969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the vehicle is a tactical kill, it's a tactical kill regardless of whether it hit a mine or hit a magical ward or whatever. The specific method of the kill is largely irrelevant. Dead is dead. An area-denial weapon (like a mine or an &quot;invisible JT trap&quot; the werewolves would use) represents fundamentally the same tactical challenge. Just because one is magic and the other isn't, how would that change the effect of battlefield doctrine? If you have a column and the vehicle in front suddenly blows up -- you stop and try to find another route around the minefield. If the vehicle instead stops suddenly and a bunch of werewolves appear out of thin air, rip the doors off the thing and <i>eat</i> the occupants -- well, probably best to go around that noise, right? Like, seriously. What's the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves don't actually need to rip the doors off. They can make them open on their own, or simply just appear inside the vehicle, because the dumbasses attacked a place with an incredibly low gauntlet. The difference is that danger cuts across dimensions; sure, an IED can happen anywhere, but werewolves turn humans into flat out prey, who no longer have access to anything that they used to in order to fight back. Not only is the vehicle gone, but so are your rifles, explosives, and all other mission equipment. What's the tactical doctrine for suddenly having all of your equipment and your armor stop functioning in the middle of the wilderness, without any safe avenues of retreat? Because I'm pretty sure it's to flee and not try the same thing twice, if you manage to make it back alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, would you rather go through that in the thing with armor, or out in the open on foot? </div> </div> </div>Not at all, because as we started off saying, assaulting caerns directly is something for which Garou, lovers of mostly straightforward attacks and Glory that they are, have likely prepared a great deal..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:33:22-07:00","id":896054,"title":"","content":"Just had a chance to see Mage20 at a friend's, it's got many rules on tech like vehicles, though I'll have to backtrack to make WW I and II planes and tanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}